Aerie-Purpose: Slide the Aerie sidebar in and out when aerie.sidebar.visible changes and resize it by drag or keys.
Aerie-Upstream-Area: chrome/browser/ui/views/frame (vertical_tab_strip_region_view.*, BUILD.gn)
Aerie-Kind: hook

Issue #177. Builds on 0024. While the layout is the sidebar the region view:

- watches aerie.sidebar.visible, slides its layer with AnimateLayer (transform and opacity only;
  opacity only under reduced motion), and takes no room in the window layout while hidden. A hide
  leaves the layout when its slide has ended, so the handler compares with the target state
  (aerie_target_visible_) and not with aerie_hidden_, and two Ctrl+S in a row stay in step with
  the pref.
- makes its resize area a "Resize sidebar" splitter. A drag has no snap points and no collapse.
  Left and Right move it 10 px (aerie_sidebar::kKeyboardResizeStep) and the new width is announced.
  The width is stored when the drag ends (through the state controller, 0025).

